# Brand

## Elements

- **Accueil lockup** — raster cropped from mockup v3 (`/brand/accueil-mark.png`
  + `/brand/accueil-wordmark.png`). SVG cannot match the fused P+arrow+U and
  the U-stem italic wordmark at Accueil size. Tagline stays HTML (i18n):
  « Organiser. Compétiter. Progresser. »
- **Chrome lockup** — same Accueil mark (arrow is a real transparency, navy
  shows through) + `/brand/accueil-wordmark-on-chrome.png` (`Play` recolored
  to `--color-on-chrome`, `'Up` unchanged). Used in the rail via
  `PlayUpLockupMark` + `PlayUpWordmark surface="chrome"`. Collapsed rail =
  mark only.
- **Chrome / favicon monogram** — `PlayUpMark` SVG for favicon, Lab optical
  sizes, and the typed wordmark proof. Geometry: `brand/monogram-geometry.ts`.
- **Typed wordmark** — `PlayUpWordmark surface="typed"`: Plex bold, 12° skew,
  `'Up` + arrow. Lab angle compare only — not product chrome.
- **Arrow / "Up"** — lockup U-stem, typed wordmark, trends. **Not** the rail
  current bar (straight 3px, Shell A).

## Angle system — **12° (arbitrated 2026-09-01)**

One angle everywhere it belongs: monogram, wordmark, trends.
**Not** the rail current indicator (straight bar, Shell A 2026-09-02).
Exposed as `--dlab-skew: -12deg` (lab) / `--brand-skew` in design-system.

Rationale: 12° survives better at small sizes (16–24px rail, trends) and reads
as a coherent system; 9° was theoretically subtler but barely perceptible in
small UI occurrences. Proof: Design Lab → **Arbitrage 9°/12°**.

`PlayUpMark` accepts `leanDeg?: 9 | 12` for the arbitration view only; product
code always uses the default **12**.

## Gradient

Allowed: Accueil lockup mark, Accueil `'Up` wordmark, Home atmosphere, chrome
monogram ≥ 24px. Never on buttons, body text, borders, badges, panels, or
page titles.

## Forbidden

- Gradient on UI chrome/controls; monogram as watermark; skewing tables/forms/panels.
- Brand blue as a status color.
- Italic wordmark as live type in chrome (rail uses the Accueil raster, not
  a skewed Plex span).
